'''Vasp Vaspar''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[Politics|politician]] who [[Senator|represented]] the [[Taldot sector]] in the [[Imperial Senate]]. He was also a member of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and served as the [[Minister of Industry]] in the [[Alliance Cabinet]], part of the [[Alliance Civil Government]]. Though he was risk averse, he was not opposed to armed conflict&mdash;but he did not believe the Alliance was capable of destroying the Empire's [[planet]]-killing [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]].

==Biography==
Vasp Vaspar was a [[Politics|politician]] who [[Senator|represented]] the [[Taldot sector]] in the [[Imperial Senate]] during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Visual Guide" /> [[Gender|He]] was known to oppose [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine's]] harshest policies.<ref name="LPOA">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref> By [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa's]] birth at [[19 BBY]]. The events of ''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]'' commence just after Organa's sixteenth [[birthday]], which places the events of the novel in [[3 BBY]].</ref> Vaspar was a regular attendee of banquets hosted on [[Alderaan]] by [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail]] and [[Breha Organa]], the [[viceroy]] and [[queen]] of the [[planet]], which secretly served as planning meetings for [[Galactic Civil War|rebellion against the Empire]].<ref name="LPOA" />

While continuing to serve in the Imperial government, he was also a member of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and served in its [[Alliance Civil Government|Civil Government]] as the [[Minister of Industry]]. This made him part of the [[Alliance Cabinet]] under the leadership of its [[Chancellor (Rebel Alliance)|Chief of State]], [[Chancellor (Rebel Alliance)|Chancellor]] [[Mon Mothma]].<ref name="Visual Guide" /> As part of his role, he attended classified Alliance Cabinet meetings concerning topics such as the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] and [[Operation Fracture]].<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref>

As Minister of Industry, Vaspar was charged with overseeing the vital yet limited resources of the fledgling Rebel Alliance. As a result of his role, he was more risk-averse than some of his fellow Alliance Cabinet members, though he was not opposed to open conflict with the Empire when warranted. However, when the Alliance learned of the Death Star, an Imperial [[superweapon]] capable of destroying entire [[planet]]s, he did not believe that the Alliance could be successful in an attack against the [[battle station]].<ref name="Visual Guide" />

Upon the [[dissolution of the Imperial Senate]], he, along with fellow former Senators [[Nower Jebel]] and [[Tynnra Pamlo]], fled to an Alliance safe world.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

==Personality and traits==
Vasp Vaspar was a [[human]] male with [[Color|black]] [[hair]], brown [[eye]]s, and light skin. The red lining on his garb denoted the [[Battle of Balamak]].<ref name="Visual Guide" />

Vaspar expressed deep concerns about the safety of [[Yavin 4]] due to the wildlife there, and was noted to have repeatedly asked for a personal [[force field]]. Mon Mothma tried her best to assuage his worries, but told [[Hendri Underholt|her aide]] to have discretion on when to say "no" to his requests for an audience, which weren't always as important as Vaspar claimed.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

==Behind the scenes==
Vasp Vaspar was a character created for the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|anthology film]], ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''. In the film, he is played by Swedish-Lebanese actor [[Fares Fares]].<ref name="Exclusive Images">{{WebCite|url=https://ew.com/gallery/rogue-one-exclusive-images|text='Rogue One: A Star Wars Story' - 15 new photos!|author=Breznican, Anthony|date=2016-11-21|work=Entertainment Weekly|archivedate=20190319020746}}</ref> The character's repetitive first name was inspired by similar redundancy in the actor's name.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/816058118467567616|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=p. 51 Senator Vaspar's repetitive first name was inspired by the actor's quite repetitive name. So why not?|archivefile=File:TwitterCap_pablohidalgo_RogueOneUVGdump.png}}</ref>

